  "selection": "November 11 was chosen because the user requested a recent completed session, before examining its results. November 10 and the freely available November 9 dated-contract sample were then added as comparison runs. No parameter optimization was performed.",
  "ruleChanges": "Existing numeric defaults retained. An implementation correction enforces the documented 60-minute five-minute-gap expiry before checking inversion; added context evidence and explicit rejection reasons. The correction did not change the six reported run outcomes.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Short-side only; entry window 09:30–11:30 New York. Candles at or after 11:30 cannot initiate a position.",
    "A: three-candle bullish five-minute gap closes through its lower edge, with a bearish fifteen-minute gap touched in the prior 60 minutes.",
    "B: bearish one-minute displacement body ≥ 8 points leaves a gap ≥ 1 point; a later bearish candle retests it.",
    "Entry at the next contiguous minute open, with 1 adverse tick; stop above the prior five one-minute highs plus 1 point.",
    "Fixed 2R price targets used because video-specific liquidity selection has not been formalized. This is a fixed-R research variant, not an exact replication of the discretionary trader.",
    "Risk $100/trade; maximum 3 MNQ; daily budget $300; $1.24 round-trip fee/contract; MNQ $2/point. These are hypotheses, not verified account costs.",
    "Stop before target if both occur in one minute; gap-through stop fills at worse open plus slippage. Target touches assumed filled at target with no queue model.",
    "Maximum drawdown is measured only at trade exits. No Topstep trailing-drawdown compliance test, spread series, partial exits, tick-order fill replay, or news filter."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three selected sessions do not establish profitability or a future edge. Comparison sessions were selected after the first run.",
    "No AI model has been trained or evaluated. A++ liquidity rules remain unverified, so no A++ performance claim is made.",
    "Data are third-party vendor observations, not an exchange-certified audit. A timestamp and OHLC check does not establish feed completeness.",
    "The free sources disagree: on November 9, 206 of 1,065 overlapping minute bars had identical OHLC; 859 differed, with a maximum field difference of 71.75 points. Sources are not pooled or treated as interchangeable.",
    "Yahoo MNQ=F does not establish a dated contract month. Yahoo research should be checked against the exact TopstepX contract before execution.",
    "The November 9 sample uses feed-receive timestamps. It confirms a separate dated-contract test, not the correctness of yesterday’s Yahoo prices."
  ],
